  "docTitle": "Amazon Locker - SDE Prep Dojo",
  "description": "Design Amazon Locker: slot sizes, best-fit allocation as a Strategy, one-time pickup codes, expiry and returns, keypad lockout and one lock per station, in Java, Python and C++14.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">Read 65 min</span><span class=\"chip\">Build 90 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Machine-coding case study</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Rank 27 of 45</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Amazon Locker</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Amazon's own favourite LLD question. A wall of doors in three sizes, a courier who needs the right door now, a customer with a six-digit code, and parcels nobody collects. We design it as an allocator with size classes, a one-time-code check and an expiry sweep, make it safe for many couriers at once, and prove it with 8 threads fighting over 600 slots. Java, Python and C++14, all compiled and run.</p>\n"
  },
